▪ Maximum-Function

▪▪ Formula

A Maximum ❗❲❳❪.tex❫❴x_{Max}❵ of a nonempty finite Collection
❗❲❳❪.tex❫❴[x_1..x_n]❵ in a totally ordered Value Domain is defined as:

❗❲❳❪.tex❫ ❴
	x_{Max} \ge x_i \quad \forall x_i \in [x_1..x_n]
❵

This Dings denotes the greatest Value, not the separate Arg-Max Operation that
returns an Input Element maximizing another Function.

▪▪ Python

▪▪▪ Function

⌜⌜⌜python
def Maximum(X1_X2_Xn_List):
	if not X1_X2_Xn_List:
		raise ValueError("Maximum requires a nonempty List")
	X_Max = X1_X2_Xn_List[0]
	for Xi in X1_X2_Xn_List[1:]:
		if Xi > X_Max:
			X_Max = Xi
	return X_Max
⌟⌟⌟

▪▪▪ Test-Case

⌜⌜⌜python
def Maximum_Test():
	X1_X2_Xn_Set = [5, 6, 3, 0, 10]
	X_Max = Maximum(X1_X2_Xn_Set)
	print(f"The Maximum of {X1_X2_Xn_Set} is {X_Max}")

Maximum_Test()
⌟⌟⌟

▪▪▪ Invocation

⌜⌜⌜python
$ python3 Maximum_Test.py
The Maximum of [5, 6, 3, 0, 10] is 10
⌟⌟⌟
